{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-115404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}\\ge 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by $(0.33)^{2x-5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5} & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} \\\\ 4{x}^{6}+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFurthermore, $4{x}^{6}+3\\ge 0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the solution is all real numbers." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge 0"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{4}{3}"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "all real numbers"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}<0.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$<x$ \n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${2}^{3x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}}{{2}^{3x}} & <\\frac{0}{{2}^{3x}} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-25)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-25 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <25 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x| & <5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $-5<x<5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278181" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6}<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${3}^{x+6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6}}{{3}^{x+6}} & <\\frac{0}{{3}^{x+6}} \\\\ (2x-5)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(2x-5)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ 2x-5 & <0 \\\\ 2x & <5 \\\\ x & <\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3<x<2"] ["math" "x<-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{5}{2}"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x<\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\frac{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}}{(0.6)^{3x-2}}<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $(0.6)^{3x-2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}}{(0.6)^{3x-2}} & <0 \\\\ (0.6)^{3x-2}\\cdot \\frac{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}}{(0.6)^{3x-2}} & <(0.6)^{3x-2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-4 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <4 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{4} \\\\ |x| & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $-2<x<2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2<x<2"] ["math" "x<-2"] ["math" "x>0"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2<x<2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $(49-{x}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}\\le 0.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${6}^{3x-2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(49-{x}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & \\le 0 \\\\ \\frac{(49-{x}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}}{{6}^{3x-2}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{6}^{3x-2}} \\\\ (49-{x}^{2})^{3} & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(49-{x}^{2})^{3}} & \\le \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ 49-{x}^{2} & \\le 0 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & \\le -49 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 49 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{49} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign again of the inequality since we divided by a negative number ($-1$).\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -7$ or $x\\ge 7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278219" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}>-{5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2}.$\n\n$x<${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x} & >-{5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2}-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+3x-10){5}^{2-7x} & >0 \\\\ (x+5)(x-2){5}^{2-7x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{2-7x}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+5)(x-2){5}^{2-7x}}{{5}^{2-7x}} & >\\frac{0}{{5}^{2-7x}} \\\\ (x+5)(x-2) & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-5$ and $x=2.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis when $x<-5$ or $x>2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/6b72efca34700ab06986460d4d190e0e83a4f0068c9effe20af622082a92b9a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x<-5$ or $x>2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-278239" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278239" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/