6\\cdot {3}^{x+1} \\\\ 5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+6+1){3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+7){3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{x+1}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+7){3}^{x+1}}{{3}^{x+1}} & <\\frac{0}{{3}^{x+1}} \\\\ 5x+7 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x & \\ge 0-7 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\ge -\\frac{7}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-278230" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278230" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278230" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278230" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}>-{6}^{3x-2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & >-{6}^{3x-2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} \\\\ 4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}+{6}^{3x-2}+{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ (4+1+{x}^{2}){6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5){6}^{3x-2} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${6}^{3x-2}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+5){6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+5 & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}^{2}+5>0$ for all values of $x,$ the solution is all real numbers." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" 