ity above is $x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -2"] ["math" "x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}"] ["math" "x\\ge 7"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-{2}^{2x-3}{x}^{2}+3x\\cdot {2}^{2x-3}>-4\\cdot {2}^{2x-3}.$\n\n{{field-1}} $<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{2}^{2x-3}{x}^{2}+3x\\cdot {2}^{2x-3} & >-4\\cdot {2}^{2x-3} \\\\ (-{x}^{2}+3x+4){2}^{2x-3} & >0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-3x-4){2}^{2x-3} & >0 \\\\ -(x+1)(x-4){2}^{2x-3} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${2}^{2x-3}$ and get\n\n$$\n-(x+1)(x-4)>0.\n$$\n\nThis represents a downwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-1$ and $x=4.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis when $-1<x<4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/df6c1c0ac26d9074f8c726b2265780fefad631561d7a729d2dfc7998ef043859.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-1<x<4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-276747" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2}<-{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <-{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+7x\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+7x)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ x(x+7)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${7}^{4x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x+7)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-7$ and $x=0.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-7<x<0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/b884ee15f864bcd02639085dc1465a82958ef0faeb9408e68b405c5906ea3a18.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-7<x<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7<x<0"] ["math" "0<x<7"] ["math" "x<0"] ["text" "$x<-7$ or $x>0$"] ["text" "$x<0$ or $x>7$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7<x<0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}\\le {4}^{4x+4}.$\n\n$x$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le {4}^{4x+4} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{4x+4} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${4}^{4x-1}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}}{{4}^{4x-1}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{4}^{4x-1}} \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5} & \\le {4}^{5} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & \\le \\sqrt[5]{{4}^{5}} \\\\ x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\le 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-278271" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{7x+2}\\le 2x\\cdot {3}^{7x+3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 2x\\cdot {3}^{7x+3} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{7x+2}-2x\\cdot {3}^{7x+3} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x\\cdot 3)\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x)\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 0 \\\\ x(x-6)\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{7x+2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-6)\\le 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=6.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis or touch this axis when $0\\le x\\le 6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/d75b387ac3e54f253eab62d9492b39f2744298e776f663d542b26e3c47f7d6a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6\\le x\\le -2"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 2"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 6"] ["text" "$x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 6$"] ["text" "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge -2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0\\le x\\le 6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-87772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${3}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\ge {3}^{4x+1}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-87772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4x}{x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{4x+1}x \\\\ {3}^{4x}{x}^{2}-{3}^{4x+1}x & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}({x}^{2}-3x) & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}x(x-3) & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{4x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-3)\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=3.$ The parabola is at or above the $x$-axis when $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/3bfb82543e7c05d0ca0b8f6c6973025400ad1253acbc57214173dbd3e8c37fef.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is  $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-87772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-87772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-87772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0\\le x\\le 3"] ["text" "$x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 0$"] ["text" "$x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3$"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-87772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{2x-7}\\ge {2}^{2x-3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{2x-7} & \\ge {2}^{2x-3} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{2x-7}-{2}^{2x-3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-{2}^{4})\\cdot {2}^{2x-7} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${2}^{2x-7}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{2}^{4}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{2}^{4} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 16 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{16} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "900404cc512731b71dd7263c5a99203d260ca5162f32ead908ae1ef64286ce7d"} {"question" "q-115450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\le x\\le 2"] ["math" "-4\\le x\\le 4"] ["math" "x\\ge 0"] ["math" "x\\le -2"] ["text" "$x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "q-115450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/state.json" "file_sha256" "2da38a6b41c2c5fbfd5fe86344c50e17da57e626196f40879080890f569ef99c"} {"question" "e-7663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(x^2-8)^3}{11^x} \\geq 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/example-7663.json" "file_sha256" "c2d14d802e3e42b8048405534c58b3ecdca34dca37517db6d089fa04c39db5ea"} {"question" "e-7663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $11^x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}}{{11}^{x}} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {11}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}}{{11}^{x}} & \\ge {11}^{x}\\cdot 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-8)^{3} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-8 & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 8 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{8} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -2\\sqrt 2$ or $x \\geq 2 \\sqrt 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/example-7663.json" "file_sha256" "c2d14d802e3e42b8048405534c58b3ecdca34dca37517db6d089fa04c39db5ea"} {"question" "e-7664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $x^2e^{x+1}-2e^{x+1} < -xe^{x+1} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/example-7664.json" "file_sha256" "e2448705d42b4a0fcebf2e24d60d7adee2351045a2007ab01ec4de356a4ed42b"} {"question" "e-7664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{x+1}-2{e}^{x+1} & <-x{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}{e}^{x+1}+x{e}^{x+1}-2{e}^{x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-2){e}^{x+1} & <0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1){e}^{x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $e^{x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-1) <   0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-2$ and $x=1.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-2 <   x <   1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/2f01104ae0cb9a41c5c5e4b8393e346f7d0e9b2bfd1afa593ee6bdfb0fff39f2.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 <   x <   1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/example-7664.json" "file_sha256" "e2448705d42b4a0fcebf2e24d60d7adee2351045a2007ab01ec4de356a4ed42b"} {"question" "e-7665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $x^5 \\cdot 4^{x} > 4^{x - 15}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/example-7665.json" "file_sha256" "fb6e2e1afc523aaf6196f6bd1d8225e820795c9750d588c24b5bf9028587f858"} {"question" "e-7665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x} & >{4}^{x-15} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x}-{4}^{x-15} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{-15})\\cdot {4}^{x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5} & >{4}^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & >\\sqrt[5]{{4}^{-15}} \\\\ x & >{({4}^{-15})}^{1/5} \\\\ x & >{4}^{-3} \\\\ x & >\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x > \\dfrac{1}{64}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/example-7665.json" "file_sha256" "fb6e2e1afc523aaf6196f6bd1d8225e820795c9750d588c24b5bf9028587f858"}] "usage" {"e-7665" [] "e-7664" [] "q-87772" [] "e-7663" []} "basis" 1328 "retractions" [[17592186157851 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3^{4x}x^{2} \\ge 3^{4x + 1}x$."] [17592186157072 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(x^2-8)^3}{11^x} \\geq 0$."] [17592186157072 :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $11^x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}((x^{2} - 8)^{3})/(11^{x}) & \\ge 0 \\\\ 11^{x} \\cdot ((x^{2} - 8)^{3})/(11^{x}) & \\ge 11^{x} \\cdot 0 \\\\ (x^{2} - 8)^{3} & \\ge 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{(x^{2} - 8)^{3}}\\begin{vmatrix}\\ge \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ x^{2} - 8\\end{vmatrix}\\ge 0; x^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\ge 8 \\\\ \\sqrt{x^{2}}\\end{vmatrix}\\ge \\sqrt{8}; \\mid x \\mid \\mid \\ge 2\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -2\\sqrt 2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2 \\sqrt 2\n$$"] [17592186157073 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x^2e^{x+1}-2e^{x+1} < -xe^{x+1}$."] [17592186157073 :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{2}e^{x + 1} - 2e^{x + 1} & < - xe^{x + 1} \\\\ x^{2}e^{x + 1} + xe^{x + 1} - 2e^{x + 1} & < 0 \\\\ (x^{2} + x - 2)e^{x + 1} & < 0 \\\\ (x + 2)(x - 1)e^{x + 1} & < 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $e^{x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-1) < 0\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-2$ and $x=1$. The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-2 < x < 1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2859/Source/Images/9bc30ffe9a0c96ace6cb684a3dbd1068.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 < x < 1$."] [17592186157074 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x^5 \\cdot 4^{x} > 4^{x - 15}$."] [17592186157074 :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{5} \\cdot 4^{x} & > 4^{x - 15} \\\\ x^{5} \\cdot 4^{x} - 4^{x - 15} & > 0 \\\\ (x^{5} - 4^{-15}) \\cdot 4^{x} & > 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{5} & > 4^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{x^{5}} & > \\sqrt[5]{4^{-15}} \\\\ x & > (4^{-15})^{1/5} \\\\ x & > 4^{-3} \\\\ x & > \\frac{1}{64}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx > \\dfrac{1}{64}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186156359 17592186156360 17592186156361 17592186156362 17592186156363] "immutable_fields" [[17592186156358 :answer-field/correct] [17592186156358 :answer-field/id] [17592186156358 :answer-field/key] [17592186156358 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
